WEBVTT

00:02:58.960 --> 00:03:00.376
And, of course, neuroscience,

00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:02.576
I've always been fascinated
with neuroscience,

00:03:02.600 --> 00:03:04.816
but I never understood
that I had to figure out

00:03:04.840 --> 00:03:06.022
why do the neurons fire,

00:03:06.046 --> 00:03:08.416
what about the environment
helps us to learn,

00:03:08.440 --> 00:03:12.696
and all of those really contribute
to making robots a little bit smarter.

00:03:12.720 --> 00:03:16.376
And so, some of the things that I do --
and this is just a little snapshot --

00:03:16.400 --> 00:03:17.936
one of the things is mirroring.

00:03:17.960 --> 00:03:21.856
So they say our ability
to look in a mirror and wave

00:03:21.880 --> 00:03:25.736
and actually recognize
that the person on the other side is us,

00:03:25.760 --> 00:03:27.136
that self-awareness,

00:03:27.160 --> 00:03:28.656
is a sign of intelligence,

00:03:28.680 --> 00:03:32.656
and that allows us
to then look at someone pitch a ball